cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GTOpt in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "GTOpt: Generation, Transmission and storage Optimization"
abstract: >-
  GTOpt (Generation, Transmission and storage Optimization; pronounced
  G-top, /ˈdʒiː tɒp/) is an open-source solver for the optimization and
  analysis of power-system generation, transmission and storage. It builds
  sparse LP/MIP formulations of multi-stage power systems for generation and
  transmission expansion planning, hydrothermal scheduling (SDDP and cascade
  decomposition), unit commitment and economic dispatch, with batteries,
  pumped hydro and reservoirs modelled as first-class storage. The acronym
  carries only the G and the T, but storage is part of the scope.
